<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Feb 7.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Feb 7.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Thursday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Portman Min	    350.79   2.21</p>
<p> 2   Mt Edon Gold	   231.87   2.11</p>
<p> 3   Niugini Min	    209.35   2.91</p>
<p> 4   Countrywide-PP	 190.32   1.18</p>
<p> 5   Mayne Nickless	 173.29   7.85</p>
<p> 6   Colonial Coml	  121.31   2.22</p>
<p> 7   Adel Bton Cement     118.12   1.63</p>
<p> 8   ST.Barbara Mine	107.04   0.76</p>
<p> 9   Forrestania Gold     102.15   2.85</p>
<p>10   Herald Rsc		88.50   1.00</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Dominion Min	     1.98   0.86</p>
<p> 2   Consol Rutile	    3.79   0.92</p>
<p> 3   Premier Inv		4.79   0.85</p>
<p> 4   BTR Plc		    6.07   5.65</p>
<p> 5   Parbury Ltd		6.67   0.79</p>
<p> 6   OLS Asia Hldgs	   6.72   0.80</p>
<p> 7   Aust Gold Rsc	    6.90   1.26</p>
<p> 8   Renison Goldflds	 7.60   5.24</p>
<p> 9   FAI Life ltd	     7.86   0.81</p>
<p>10   Templeton Global	 7.94   1.39</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
